Copy Compiler and Build Tools from Gentoo Host

1. Copy core build executables:

`cp -av /usr/bin/gcc $KLFS/usr/bin/`
`cp -av /usr/bin/g++ $KLFS/usr/bin/`
`cp -av /usr/bin/make $KLFS/usr/bin/`
`cp -av /usr/bin/as $KLFS/usr/bin/`
`cp -av /usr/bin/ld $KLFS/usr/bin/`

2. Symlink binaries to standard locations:

`ln -sf /usr/bin/gcc $KLFS/bin/cc`
`ln -sf /usr/bin/make $KLFS/bin/make`

3. Copy toolchain shared libraries:

`cp -av /usr/lib64/libgmp.so* $KLFS/usr/lib64/`
`cp -av /usr/lib64/libmpfr.so* $KLFS/usr/lib64/`
`cp -av /usr/lib64/libmpc.so* $KLFS/usr/lib64/`
`cp -av /usr/lib64/libz.so* $KLFS/usr/lib64/`
`cp -av /usr/lib64/libzstd.so* $KLFS/usr/lib64/`

4. Copy GCC internal headers and CRTs (critical for linking):

`cp -av --parents /usr/lib/gcc $KLFS/`
`cp -av --parents /usr/include $KLFS/`
